---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ConsentManager from '../components/react/privacy/ConsentManager';
import ForgetMeButton from '../components/react/privacy/ForgetMeButton';

//Privacy & cookie policy — static Astro page; the interactive controls (live
//analytics-consent toggle + forget-me) are React islands. Ads consent is
//gathered by Google's certified CMP. Legal basis: GDPR Art. 6(1)(a) + ZZPL.
const LAST_UPDATED = '2026-08-19';
const CONTACT = 'privacy@ranklock.app';

//Analytics rows are first-party, set only after the banner grant; Ads rows are
//set by Google under its own consent message.
const cookies = [
  ['_pk_id', 'Analytics', 'Matomo', "Persistent visitor ID — groups your visits so repeat visits don't count as new visitors", '13 months'],
  ['_pk_ses', 'Analytics', 'Matomo', 'Active-session marker — tells Matomo the current visit is still ongoing', '30 minutes'],
  ['_pk_ref', 'Analytics', 'Matomo', 'Remembers which referrer originally brought you to the site', '6 months'],
  ['__gads', 'Ads', 'Google AdSense', 'Ad delivery, frequency capping and aggregated ad reporting', 'up to 13 months'],
  ['__gpi', 'Ads', 'Google AdSense', 'Stores an ad-personalization identifier used by Google', 'up to 13 months'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy & cookies — RankLock"
  description="What RankLock collects, why, how long it is kept, and how to change or withdraw your consent at any time. Self-hosted analytics, GDPR + Serbian ZZPL."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <main class="container" style="padding-top:40px; padding-bottom:64px;">
    <div class="legal">
      <div class="kicker" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Last updated · {LAST_UPDATED}</div>
      <h1 class="h-hero" style="font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,48px); margin-bottom:14px;">Privacy &amp; cookies</h1>
      <p style="font-size:16px; color:var(--text-2); max-width:72ch; margin-bottom:8px;">
        RankLock keeps data handling small and explicit. This page tells you exactly what is
        collected, why, how long it sticks around, and how to make it stop. Analytics never
        load until you choose on the consent banner, and ads are served by Google under its
        own consent message. If anything here is unclear, write to
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who runs this site</h2>
      <div class="dualcard" style="margin:8px 0 4px;">
        <div class="dc-label">Data controller</div>
        <p style="margin:0;">
          RankLock is an independent, unofficial Deadlock statistics project operated from
          Serbia. The operator is the sole data controller. There is no company behind the
          site, no co-controllers, and no third-party processors beyond the infrastructure
          and ad providers named in sections 4 and 10. Contact:
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>2. What data is collected</h2>
      <p>With <strong>analytics</strong> consent enabled, a self-hosted Matomo instance records:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pageviews</strong> — which pages you opened and in what order</li>
        <li><strong>Referrers</strong> — the link or search result that sent you here (if any)</li>
        <li><strong>Country</strong> — derived from an anonymized IP (the last two bytes are stripped before storage)</li>
        <li><strong>Device basics</strong> — screen size, browser name, operating-system family</li>
        <li><strong>Session duration</strong> — how long the visit lasted</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Google AdSense may serve ads and set its own cookies (section 4) to deliver, cap and
        measure them. Visitors in the EEA, UK and Switzerland are asked about ads by Google's
        own consent message, not by this site's banner. RankLock does not receive your
        identity from Google; it receives only aggregate ad-performance reporting.
      </p>

      <h2>3. What is NOT collected</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No names, email addresses, or user accounts</strong> — there are no logins on the stats surface</li>
        <li><strong>No analytics before you consent</strong> — Matomo loads and sets cookies only after you accept analytics on the banner</li>
        <li><strong>No selling or sharing of analytics data</strong> — Matomo data stays on our own server and is never handed to third parties</li>
        <li><strong>No heatmaps, session replay, or fingerprinting</strong></li>
        <li><strong>No analytics signal to Google</strong> — Google Consent Mode's <code>analytics_storage</code> is left denied; ad consent signals are managed by Google's consent message</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Cookies used</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics cookies are set <strong>only after</strong> you grant analytics consent on
        the banner; they are first-party (this domain). Ad cookies are set by Google AdSense
        under the choice you make in Google's own consent message.
      </p>
      <table class="ctable">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Name</th><th>Category</th><th>Set by</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {cookies.map(([name, cat, by, purpose, life]) => (
            <tr>
              <td><b>{name}</b></td>
              <td>{cat}</td>
              <td>{by}</td>
              <td>{purpose}</td>
              <td>{life}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        Your consent choice and your theme preference are stored in this browser's
        <code>localStorage</code> (keys <code>ranklock-consent</code> and
        <code>ranklock-theme</code>), not in cookies, and never leave your device.
        Clearing the cookies above detaches you from any existing analytics record.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        RankLock has visitors from both Serbia and the EU/EEA, so both frameworks apply. In
        both, the basis is the same: your explicit consent, given through the banner.
      </p>
      <div class="dualcol">
        <div class="dualcard">
          <div class="dc-label">Visitors in Serbia</div>
          <p style="margin:0;">
            Processing is based on your unambiguous consent under the Serbian Law on Personal
            Data Protection (Zakon o zaštiti podataka o ličnosti). You can withdraw consent at
            any time using the controls in section 7, and withdrawal is as easy as giving it.
          </p>
          <div class="dc-cite"><b>Art. 12 ZZPL</b> — consent</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dualcard">
          <div class="dc-label">Visitors in the EU / EEA</div>
          <p style="margin:0;">
            Processing is based on your freely given, specific, informed and unambiguous
            consent under the GDPR. The same withdrawal controls apply, and withdrawing
            consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing before the withdrawal.
          </p>
          <div class="dc-cite"><b>Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR</b> — consent</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under both the GDPR and the Serbian ZZPL you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access</strong> — ask what data, if any, is tied to your visitor ID</li>
        <li><strong>Rectification</strong> — correct inaccurate data</li>
        <li><strong>Deletion</strong> — ask that records tied to your visitor ID be removed</li>
        <li><strong>Restriction</strong> — ask that processing of your records be paused</li>
        <li><strong>Objection</strong> — object to the processing described here</li>
        <li><strong>Data portability</strong> — receive your records in a machine-readable export</li>
        <li><strong>Withdrawal of consent</strong> — revoke consent at any time (section 7)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. Because
        analytics data is pseudonymous — tied to a cookie-held visitor ID, not a name — please
        include the value of your <code>_pk_id</code> cookie so the right records can be found.
        Under GDPR Art. 11 (and the ZZPL equivalent) we are not required to collect extra
        identifying data just to answer a request; clearing your <code>_pk_*</code> cookies
        detaches you from any future session regardless.
      </p>

      <h2 id="consent">7. Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        Turn analytics on or off at any time, and erase the data already stored about this
        browser. Changes take effect immediately — no reload needed. Ads personalization is
        managed in Google's consent message, not on this page.
      </p>
      <ConsentManager client:load />
      <ForgetMeButton client:load />

      <h2>8. Right to complain</h2>
      <p>If you believe your data has been handled improperly, you can complain to your supervisory authority.</p>
      <div class="dualcol">
        <div class="dualcard">
          <div class="dc-label">If you are in Serbia</div>
          <p style="margin:0;">File with the Commissioner for Information of Public Importance and Personal Data Protection (Poverenik).</p>
          <div class="dc-cite"><a href="https://www.poverenik.rs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">poverenik.rs →</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dualcard">
          <div class="dc-label">If you are in the EU / EEA</div>
          <p style="margin:0;">File with your national Data Protection Authority. The full list is maintained by the European Data Protection Board.</p>
          <div class="dc-cite"><a href="https://edpb.europa.eu/about-edpb/about-edpb/members_en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">edpb.europa.eu →</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>9. Retention periods</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Raw analytics logs</strong> — deleted after <strong>12 months</strong>; the Matomo server auto-removes raw visit rows at that age</li>
        <li><strong>Aggregated reports</strong> — retained for <strong>24 months</strong>; anonymous traffic summaries with no record-level detail</li>
        <li><strong>Consent records</strong> — kept for the duration of your consent plus <strong>2 years</strong>, so a regulator asking "did you have consent on date X" can be answered</li>
        <li><strong>Ad cookies</strong> — governed by Google's retention for the cookies in section 4; cleared when you change your choice in Google's consent message or clear cookies</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>10. Where the data lives</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Analytics stored in the EU/EEA</strong> on self-operated infrastructure (Hetzner, Germany) — no managed-analytics SaaS</li>
        <li><strong>Ad serving by Google</strong> under its own terms and its own consent message; see Google's privacy &amp; ads policies</li>
        <li><strong>Encrypted backups</strong> are GPG-encrypted locally before upload, so the storage provider never sees plaintext</li>
        <li><strong>No transfer of analytics data to third parties</strong> beyond the infrastructure provider</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>11. Last updated</h2>
      <p>
        This policy was last updated on <strong>{LAST_UPDATED}</strong>. Material changes will
        be noted here with a new date; trivial copy edits do not bump the date.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
